        <p>I\TOTICE IS HEREBY GIVEN, that the next GEN- ERAL QUARTER SESSIONS ,f the Peace for the COUNTY OF CHESTER will be opened at the COURT HOUSE, NETHER KNUTSFORD, in and for the said County, on MONDAY, the 3rd day of April next, at half- past Eleven o'clock in the Forenoon, but in consequence of that day being a Bank Holiday the business of the Court will be adjourned to the following day at the same time, when the Grand Jury will be empancelled. The hearing of the Appeals arising within the Hundreds of Bucklow, Macclesfield and Northwich, forming the Knutsford District, and the trials ofp al} prisoners com- mitted from such Hundreds, will take piece at such Sessions. The Grand and Petty Juries for the Knutsford District must be in attendance at the Court House, Knutsford, on TUESDAY, the 4th day of April next, at Half-past Eleven o'clock in the Forenoon. THE Court will be adjourned to the Castle of Chester, on THURSDAY, the 6th day of April next, at Eleven o'clock in the Forenoon. The hearing of all Appeals arising within the Hundreds of Broxten, Eddisbury, Nantwich and Wirral, forming the Chester District, and the trials of all prisoners committed from the last-men- tioned Hundreds will take place at such adjourned Ses- sions. The Grand and Petty Juries for the Chester District must be in attendance at the Castle of Chester, at the opening of the Court on THURSDAY, the 6th day of April next, at Eleven o'clock in the Forenoon. REGINALD POTTS. Clerk of the Peace for the County of Chester. Chester, 13th March, 1893.</p>
