        <p>SHOCKING CRUELTY BY A STEPMOTHER. At Leicester Police Court, on Thursday, a woman named Joyce, aged 45, was c barged with cruelty to two little girls, her stepdaughters. The evidence of the girls and neighbours showed that the children had been repeatedly beaten. They had been severely bruised and their hair pulled out, while a poker had been pushed into the eye of the elder, and the elbow of the younger cut with a knife. The defendant denied the charge, but was sentenced to 21 days' hard labour. THE BOTTLEMAKERS' APPEAL. The officials of the Lancashire district of the Glass Bottle Makers' Trade Protection Association have issued an appeal to men of other trades, in the hope that con- tributions will be freely given to aid them while on strike. It is stated that this is the first appeal for thirty-five years, during which time they have contri- buted no less than £B,OOO to ether trades in their dis- tress. The object of the strike is (the circular states) to resist a reduction of about 83. per week. Everything is quiet in St. Ile:ens and Newton, and no negociations have been made towards a settlement.</p>
