        <p>PENKETH. FOOTBALL: FBNEETH VILLAGE v. FIVIEN.D&amp; SCHOOL.— This match was played on the school ground on Netur- day, before a good number of spectators. The village started off with the wind and sun in their faces. After half-an-hour's play the school scored the first goal, but the village equalised a few minutos hater. The school again scored, thus leading by two to one at half time. On restarting the village had matters all their own way, Dumbell and G. Boyer scoring two each, while Moore and the two full backs, Elliot and Lewis, scored thus leaving Penketh Village winners by seven goals to three. DISCOVERY OF CANNEL COAL IN FLINTSHIRE. Great rejoicings have been caused throughout the Leeswood colliery district of Flintsiaire by the aunounce- ment that Messrs. Chandler have it length succeeded in driving into the cannel seams in their secon4 adit. These seams are four feet six inohos in thickness, and are of great value for gas making purposes. In a very short , time the company will give employukeat tct addktional men.</p>
